robot: open_duck_mini_zp10d | consumers: Placo/Pinocchio reference planning, CAD Viewer
units: metres, kg, seconds, radians | root axes: +X eyes/forward, +Y left, +Z up
source: xmls/open_duck_mini_zp10d.xml SHA256 12a9ca61f0c10bc320f6eecc8517bad557e0d89dc64500fcfb191d9dadbfd8d0
source scene: xmls/scene_flat_terrain.xml, accepted shortened legs and 60-degree home
root: base, frame-only; floating-base transform is supplied by Placo (no world joint)
physical links: source MJCF bodies below base; link/joint names and zero poses preserved
trunk: source trunk site, frame-only; left_foot/right_foot: frame-only sole references
sole frames: source foot site XY; Z projected onto minimum collision-vertex height at home
sole orientation: body Rx(-pi/2), yielding forward X, left Y, up Z at home
meshes: explicit sets of original per-solid visual STLs; already metres, scale 1
visual origins: copied raw MJCF geom transforms (not compiled mesh-normalization offsets)
collision: intentionally omitted for this kinematic planner; full MJCF owns contact validation
inertials: source per-body CAD-derived estimates, copied COM/full inertia in body frame
mass: estimated PETG/purchased masses; not weighed or calibrated to actual infill
limits/axis: copied source hinge ranges and local axes; positive is right-hand about axis
effort: copied actuator force limits; velocity 5.24 rad/s is original software cap, uncalibrated
antenna axes are oblique by measured CAD design; retained without snapping to principal axes
frame-only links omit inertia/geometry; no fake mass is introduced
joint ledger: parent/child/origin/axis are explicit in each joint below
positive axes at accepted home, expressed in world:
